  "name": "Turbine Sport",
  "author": "whirligig",
  "version": "1",
  "notes": "A kerosene micro-turbine sport jet: 90 N of thrust, 8 kg, and a tank that empties in about five minutes at full power. The turbine is not modelled as a thrust number but as a momentum machine \u2014 it swallows air at the flight speed and throws it out at roughly 520 m/s \u2014 so the thrust lapse with speed and with altitude falls out rather than being tabulated. Raise `bypassRatio` and the same core spreads its power over more air: the jet slows, static thrust rises and the thrust falls away faster with speed, which is the whole turbojet-versus-turbofan trade in one number. The thing that makes it fly like a turbine rather than a fan is `spoolTime`: three seconds from idle to full, so the throttle has to be planned rather than used. Datum is the wing quarter chord.",
